Base model
----------

This model is a modified version of the tessdata_best Hebrew model
(heb.traineddata) of the Tesseract OCR project,
https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best, commit
e12c65a915945e4c28e237a9b52bc4a8f39a0cec, sha256
dbaa827aea6bc21215638447f17783a1004987c2d0bf5573d111fee397abdae5, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

HeOCR modified it on 2026-11-18: its LSTM network was fine-tuned with
Tesseract's lstmtraining on synthetic office-document lines, rendered
born-digital lines and real scanned lines. Its character set and its
dictionary components are the base model's, unchanged. No word list was
built from any training text.

Software
--------

The model was trained with, and runs in, Tesseract 5.5.3
(https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. The model file contains no Tesseract code.

Training data: Reshumot (laws and regulations)
----------------------------------------------

Training lines were rendered by HeOCR from born-digital PDF booklets of
ספר החוקים (Sefer ha-Hukim) and קובץ התקנות (Kovetz ha-Takanot), published
by Reshumot (רשומות), the official gazette of the State of Israel, and
labelled with the publisher's own PDF text layer for each line. The same
text was laid out again in HeOCR's synthetic office pages. Further training
lines are scans of Reshumot booklets. Laws and regulations carry no
copyright in Israel (Copyright Act 2007, section 6; PD-IL). Their status
outside Israel, including the United States, is not asserted here. No line
comes from an evaluation booklet. The booklet identifiers are in
modern_v1_training_run.json.

Training data: Hebrew Wikisource (text)
---------------------------------------

The labels of 58,658 scanned Reshumot training lines (line set
olbreshumotlines_v1) are the same-wording text of ספר החוקים הפתוח (the
Open Law Book) on Hebrew Wikisource, by Hebrew Wikisource contributors,
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence
(CC BY-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Each page's
revision id and permalink is listed in modern_v1_training_run.json. Per heocr-engine decision 0016 the weights
stay Apache-2.0 with this credit, and no word list or dawg was built from
Wikisource text: the model's word list is the base model's.

